V3 -- VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
V1 -- per-cluster r_knee/R_cap (the new scatter) vs r_knee/r_M:
     [canonical] r_b/R_cap median 0.44 (range 0.27-1.26) vs r_b/rM median 0.43 (old scalar); r_on/R_cap median 1.21 vs r_on/rM 1.16
     [alt] r_b/R_cap median 0.54 (range 0.35-1.92) vs r_b/rM median 0.53 (old scalar); r_on/R_cap median 1.50 vs r_on/rM 1.47
V2 -- the delta chi2 at the R_cap-class break:
     [canonical] split-vs-floor (R_cap firing rule) REG 50-600 pooled +51235.4; two-zone fix-at-R_cap median delta 29.1 (fix-at-rM 24.6)
     [alt] split-vs-floor (R_cap firing rule) REG 50-600 pooled +44087.4; two-zone fix-at-R_cap median delta 91.7 (fix-at-rM 96.7)
V3 -- the honest statement:
     FAILS TOO: the model-free knee sits at r_b/R_cap = 0.44 (canonical) / 0.54 (alt) -- a factor ~2 INSIDE the theory's operative cap, NOT ~1; fixing the phantom turn-on at R_cap costs a median delta chi2 of 29 (canonical) / 92 (alt) per cluster -- the same order as D036's fix-at-r_M failure (24.6 / 96.7).  AND the re-prediction is nearly DEGENERATE with the old test: D036's r_M was already the total-field a0-crossing (r_M/R_cap = 1.00-1.05), so the 'wrong radius' diagnosis is itself wrong -- hy4 never used the 274-580 kpc baryon-scale r_M.  The knee (rb 173-603 kpc) is interior to BOTH the a0-crossing class (R_cap 476-958) and NFW's own -2 crossing (r = rs; r_b/rs ~ 0.54) -- nearer the NFW scale radius than the cap, but at neither prediction.  hy4's break failure stands; the cap-break re-prediction resolves nothing on the committed data alone.


